  "fidelity": {
    "functional": {
      "claims": "Nets, ports, LEDs and the reset button as logic-level parts; the ATmega328P runs its firmware (see its description). The ATmega16U2 bridge is a serial port on the host (a pseudo-terminal): the host program's baud rate is the line's, a mismatch with the sketch's decodes as garbage both ways, and opening the port (DTR raised) resets the ATmega328P as the 100 nF auto-reset capacitor does.",
      "omissions": [
        "the 16U2's bytes reach USART0 directly, not as frames on PD0 through its 1 kOhm resistors (a shield driving D0 does not contend with it)",
        "DTR toggled by ioctl (avrdude's arduino programmer), RTS and breaks: a pseudo-terminal has no modem lines",
        "Optiboot: the board is programmed by the session, not through the bridge (ADR-031)",
        "the TX and RX LEDs",
        "the LMV358 buffer on the L LED",
        "ICSP headers"
      ],
      "validation": [
        "tests/*.json"
      ]
    },
    "timed": {
      "claims": "As functional.",
      "omissions": [
        "as functional"
      ],
      "validation": [
        "tests/*.json"
      ]
    },
    "electrical": {
      "claims": "Regulators, LEDs with series resistors, the reset pull-up and the resonator as BVD equivalents; GPIO bridges use the MCU's pin-model defaults. USB's 5 V arrives on USB_VBUS through F1 (the MF-MSMF050-2 resettable fuse, which heats and trips above about 1 A) and T1 (the FDN340P switch) to +5V; U5A (LMV358) compares VIN/2 with 3.3 V and turns T1 off when VIN is above about 6.6 V, so the regulator supplies the board and USB carries nothing.",
      "omissions": [
        "decoupling",
        "the reset capacitor's waveform (its reset is a pulse, the DTR reset above)",
        "ESD diodes",
        "the L LED is driven from D13 itself: U5B follows D13 without the LED as its load",
        "the LMV358 below its 2.7 V minimum supply (after F1 trips) behaves as the model extrapolates, not as a real part does",
        "the 3V3 regulator is modelled as an LM1117-3.3 (1.2 V dropout), not the R3's LP2985-33"
      ],
      "validation": [
        "tests/*.json"
      ]
    }
  },
